### =============================================
### JWT Flow Testing - ShopEase User Service
### Tool: VS Code "REST Client" extension
###        or IntelliJ HTTP Client (built-in)
### Base URL: http://localhost:8081
### =============================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8081/api

### ----- REGISTER FLOW -----

### Test R3: Register Success (Happy Path - Auto Login)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "testuser@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "fullName": "Test User",
  "phone": "+84900000000"
}

### Test R1: Register - Payload Invalid (missing required fields)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-valid-email",
  "password": "123"
}

### Test R2: Register - Email Already Exists
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "buyer@shopease.local",
  "password": "password123",
  "fullName": "Duplicate User"
}

### ----- LOGIN FLOW -----

### Login - Happy Path (Buyer)
# @name loginBuyer
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "buyer@shopease.local",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Login - Happy Path (Seller)
# @name loginSeller
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "seller@shopease.local",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Login - Wrong Email
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nonexistent@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Login - Wrong Password
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "buyer@shopease.local",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

### ----- SAVE TOKENS FROM LOGIN RESPONSE -----
### After running "Login - Happy Path (Buyer)", copy the tokens here:

@accessToken = PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE
@refreshToken = PASTE_REFRESH_TOKEN_HERE

### ----- REFRESH TOKEN FLOW -----

### Test F5: Refresh - Happy Path
### (After this, the old refreshToken is REVOKED. Save the new RT!)
# @name refreshHappy
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### Test F4: Refresh - Reuse Detection (use OLD refreshToken again)
### This should FAIL and revoke the entire token family!
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### Test F1: Refresh - Malformed/Fake Token
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJmYWtlLXVzZXIifQ.invalid-signature"
}

### Test F2: Refresh - Valid JWT but not in DB
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "not-even-a-jwt-token"
}

### ----- LOGOUT FLOW -----

### Logout - Single Device
### (Login again first to get fresh tokens, then paste refreshToken here)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### Verify: Try to refresh after logout (should fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### ----- LOGOUT ALL DEVICES -----

### Logout All - Requires valid Access Token
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout-all
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Verify: Use old AT after logout-all (should fail with token_version mismatch)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout-all
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### ----- PROTECTED API (User Profile) -----

### Get User Profile with valid AT
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Get User Profile without AT (Case A1)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me

### Get User Profile with invalid AT (Case A2)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer invalid.token.here

### ----- TEST VIA GATEWAY (port 8080) -----
### Uncomment these if Gateway is running

# @gatewayUrl = http://localhost:8080/api

### Login via Gateway
# POST {{gatewayUrl}}/auth/login
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# {
#   "email": "buyer@shopease.local",
#   "password": "password123"
# }

### Access protected resource via Gateway
# GET {{gatewayUrl}}/users/me
# Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
